<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Crisis</p><h1 class="enc-title">July Crisis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1914</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The July Crisis was the diplomatic crisis of 1914 following the assassination of Archduke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archduke-franz-ferdinand-of-austria">Franz Ferdinand</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarajevo">Sarajevo</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a> issued an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-ultimatum-to-serbia">ultimatum to Serbia</a>, and alliances drew the great powers into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. The war led to the collapse of the Austro-Hungarian Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/july-crisis.jpg" alt="July Crisis" width="292" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Willibald Krain (1886–1945) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Der_St%C3%A4nker.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
